  },
  "description": "Modular MCP SDK shared across all Burdenoff product MCPs (vibecontrols, botlit, fluidgrids, bigconsole, healthybowl, workspaces). Each module exports an McpModule contract; product MCPs become thin shells that pick which modules to mount.",
  "dist-tags": {
   "alpha": "2026.523.1",
   "latest": "2026.908.2"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/algoshred/mcp-libs#readme",
  "keywords": [
   "burdenoff",
   "mcp",
   "model-context-protocol",
   "mcp-sdk",
   "modular",
   "graphql"
  ],
  "license": "UNLICENSED",
  "maintainers": [
   {
    "email": "[redacted-email:4e43850fb445]",
    "name": "burdenoffcorp"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@burdenoff/mcp-libs",
  "readme": "# @burdenoff/mcp-libs\n\nModular MCP SDK shared across all Burdenoff product MCPs.\n\nEach module under `src/modules/<name>/` exports an `McpModule`. Product MCPs become thin shells (~125 lines) that pick which modules to mount, build an `McpContext`, pick a transport, and ship the binary.\n\n## Status \u2014 `1.0.0`\n\n23 modules cover the full surface of `vibecontrols-app`'s microfrontends (~317 tools / 7 resources / 7 prompts):\n\n| Domain | Modules |\n|---|---|\n| Identity | `auth` (full surface incl. mfa, api-keys, sso, delegations), `rbac`, `organizations`, `tours` |\n| Workspace primitives | `workspaces`, `groups`, `tags`, `files`, `conversations`, `security` |\n| Operations | `integrations`, `channels`, `scheduler`, `export`, `notifications`, `support`, `products`, `devportal` |\n| Commerce | `billing`, `store` |\n| Product surface | `vibecontrols` (rich; 16 sub-entities), `sandbox`, `health` |\n\nMounted in 6 product MCPs: `vibecontrols`, `botlit`, `fluidgrids`, `bigconsole`, `healthybowl`, `workspaces` \u2014 each consumes the same 23-module catalogue with product-prefixed tool names via `mcpToolName(productName, \u2026)`.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nbun add @burdenoff/mcp-libs @modelcontextprotocol/sdk graphql graphql-request zod\n```\n\nFor HTTP transport:\n\n```bash\nbun add express cors\n```\n\n## Quick start (product MCP shell)\n\n```ts\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { buildContext, createMcpServer } from '@burdenoff/mcp-libs/core';\nimport { startStdioServer, startHttpServer } from '@burdenoff/mcp-libs/transports';\nimport authModule from '@burdenoff/mcp-libs/modules/auth';\nimport vibecontrolsModule from '@burdenoff/mcp-libs/modules/vibecontrols';\n// ... import the rest of the 23 modules as needed\nimport pkg from '../package.json' with { type: 'json' };\n\nconst ctx = buildContext({\n  productName: 'vibecontrols',\n  productVersion: pkg.version,\n  serverName: 'vibecontrols-mcp',\n  serverVersion: pkg.version,\n  defaults: {\n    configDirName: 'vibecontrols-mcp',\n    oidcClientId: 'burdenoff_mcp_vibecontrols',\n    workspaceEndpointDefault: 'http://localhost:4003/workspaces/graphql',\n    globalEndpointDefault: 'http://localhost:4000/global/graphql',\n    httpPortDefault: 3000,\n  },\n});\n\nconst server = createMcpServer(ctx, [authModule, vibecontrolsModule], {\n  name: 'vibecontrols-mcp',\n  version: pkg.version,\n});\n\nawait startStdioServer(server, ctx);\n```\n\n## Repository layout\n\n- `src/core/` \u2014 `McpModule`, `McpContext`, error classes, gql client, auth, config, output helpers.\n- `src/transports/` \u2014 stdio + HTTP transport factories (express dynamic-imported).\n- `src/modules/<name>/` \u2014 one folder per module: `index.ts` (McpModule export), `tools.ts`, `resources.ts` (optional), `prompts.ts` (optional), `operations.ts`.\n\nSee [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md) for the full architecture, hard rules, and adding-a-module guide.\n\n## License\n\nUNLICENSED \u2014 Burdenoff Consultancy Services Pvt. Ltd.\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
  "repository": {
   "type": "git",
   "url": "git+https://github.com/algoshred/mcp-libs.git"
  },
